  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "In the isosceles triangle $ABC$, the measure of $\\angle B$ is $50^\\circ$. Find all possible measures of $\\angle A$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$50^\\circ$, $65^\\circ$ or $80^\\circ$.\n\nConsider each possible pair of equal angles.",
      "worked": "If $\\angle A=\\angle B$, then $\\angle A=50^\\circ$.\n\nIf $\\angle A=\\angle C$,\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\angle A+50^\\circ&=180^\\circ\\\\2\\angle A&=130^\\circ\\\\\\angle A&=65^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nIf $\\angle B=\\angle C$, then $\\angle C=50^\\circ$ and\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle A&=180^\\circ-50^\\circ-50^\\circ\\\\\\angle A&=80^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\angle A$ can be $50^\\circ$, $65^\\circ$ or $80^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
